<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="210f9c3e">&lt;p&gt;
    Multiple test scenarios can be created for a single requirement, business process, use case or user story. Test
    scenarios typically have a one-to-many relationship with test cases.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="503b62e1"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="a30793ad"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="cfb23c8f">&lt;p&gt;
    As an example, the test scenarios outlined below capture the various aspects of functionality to test for the
    given requirement:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        A customer can login to an ecommerce website with a valid username and password
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Test Scenarios&lt;/u&gt;:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            Validate that only registered users are allowed to login
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            Validate that unregistered users are asked to register
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            Validate that only registered users can request a password reset&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
